WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.373
If you find yourself going into a freefall

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:07.807
inside a metal tube,

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:08.975
hurtling through the clouds

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:11.011
at hundreds of kilometers per hour,

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.113
and an oxygen mask drops down

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.080
right in front of you -

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.815
try not to panic. 

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.418
Airplane crashes are highly survivable.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.819
And here's what you can do

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.955
to increase your chances of survival...

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.160
Taking a flight on a
commercial airplane

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.397
is about as risky as riding an escalator.

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:32.565
The odds of being
killed in a plane crash

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.667
are 1 in 11 million.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.936
You're more likely to
drown in a bubble bath,

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.872
choke on your breakfast, or...

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:42.142
die in a car accident
on your way to the airport.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:45.779
Yet, we can all feel a little
nervous when stepping on a plane.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.259
Here are 6 things you can do

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:00.894
to survive a plane crash.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.068
Your flip-flops may be comfy,

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.636
but they're not going to perform well

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.337
in case of an emergency.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.940
And neither will your high-heeled shoes.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.576
The National Transportation
Safety Board reports that

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.179
68% of passengers in plane accidents

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:22.182
die from injuries in post-crash fires.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:25.285
So go for long pants
and long-sleeved shirts -

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:28.221
they'll protect you from
flames and sharp objects.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:32.192
And put on lace-up shoes,
in case you need to run.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.233
Where is the safest
place to sit, anyway?

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:44.204
According to an analysis of airplane
crashes by Popular Mechanics,

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:47.674
your best bet is to sit as far
back in the airplane as possible.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:50.910
Unless the plane goes down tail-first. 

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:54.647
You see, there is no such thing
as the safest seat on a plane.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.717
It all really depends on the situation.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.719
Regardless of what
section you're sitting in,

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.322
know where the emergency exits are.

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.756
When you get on the plane,

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:07.060
count the rows to the closest
one so that you can find it

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.330
even if the cabin is filled with smoke.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.336
The first three minutes after takeoff

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.271
and the eight minutes before landing

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:21.808
are the most accident-prone
times of the entire flight.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.710
Make sure to keep your shoes on,

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.145
your seatbelt fastened

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.213
and your tray table up.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.049
Put your carry-on items
under the seat in front of you.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.217
You know why?

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:34.554
To keep your legs from going
under the seat and getting broken.

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:37.390
And pay attention to the
emergency instructions,

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:40.393
even if you've been on a
plane many times before -

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.362
not all planes are the same.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:51.905
The first 90 seconds of a plane
crash are the most important.

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.306
Many people get so nervous

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.775
they forget how to
unbuckle their seatbelt.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.844
Listen carefully to the instructions.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.979
But don't just sit through the disaster

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.948
waiting for orders if they are not coming.

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:05.585
The first thing you should
do is to prepare for impact.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:08.121
Bend over, grab your
legs behind your knees

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.989
and keep your head down.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.457
In the worst-case scenario,

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:14.160
the cabin will experience
sudden pressure loss

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.062
and oxygen deficiency.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:19.632
You'll only have about 10 seconds
before you go unconscious.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.235
So if you see the oxygen
masks drop down,

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.204
put one on yourself first.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.773
Only then should you try
to help someone else.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.680
If you get to evacuate from the plane,

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.648
do it as quickly as possible.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.650
Don't try to get your
carry-on to take with you -

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.285
in the time you waste,
you might end up

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:42.455
getting stuck with it on a burning plane.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.795
If your plane hits the ground,

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:51.264
there's a high chance of it exploding.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:54.267
Run - at least 150 meters
(500 feet) away from it

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.369
in the direction against the wind,

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:59.072
and wait for the rescuers to find you.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:01.341
It's good to be prepared for anything.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:03.343
But don't be afraid of flying.

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:07.914
In the history of aviation, it's
never been a safer time to fly.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:11.117
Commercial aviation averages
less than 500 fatalities

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:13.419
per year worldwide.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.521
Among planes that
do get into accidents,

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:19.158
over 95% of the passengers
get out of them alive.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:22.962
Personally, I try to think of
turbulence like bumps on the road.

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.831
Helps with my flying anxiety.

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.966
That's a little tip from me to you.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.402
Stay tuned for another how to...

